ary\":\"КП+УО is the preferred controlled-rolling plus accelerated-cooling scheme\",\"explanation\":\"КП+УО is a high-temperature controlled-rolling scheme combining controlled rolling with accelerated cooling. It uses 8 finishing-stand passes at temperatures 30–50 °C higher than ordinary controlled rolling, followed by accelerated cooling on УОВТ at 10–30 °C/s to 500–550 °C. The scheme is identified as preferred because its finishing-stand sheet rolling duration is shorter by 50 s or more than 1.5 times compared with КП+УО+КП, and by 150 s compared with low-temperature КП. КП is a stage within the КП+УО route. [Data: Entities (1565, 1350, 1686, 1699, 1700, +more); Relationships (3202, 3348, 3412, 3459, 3460, +more)]\"},{\"summary\":\"УОВТ is the accelerated-cooling unit enabling these schemes\",\"explanation\":\"УОВТ (UOVT) is the accelerated-cooling installation at mill 3600, also called установка УОВТ. It performs forced cooling of rolled stock after rolling, including intermediate cooling from 820–870 °C to 700–750 °C and accelerated cooling at 10–30 °C/s to 500–550 °C. The unit is used in the КП+УО+КП scheme for intermediate cooling and in KPUO/КП+УО for accelerated cooling. Its achieved cooling rates fall within the required temperature interval and meet stated cooling-rate and cooling-duration requirements. [Data: Entities (1418, 1381, 1357, 1777, 1797, +more); Relationships (3561, 3016, 3271, 3374, 3211, +more)]\"},{\"summary\":\"КП+УО+КП adds intermediate cooling and controlled rolling\",\"explanation\":\"КП+УО+КП is a high-temperature scheme comprising controlled rolling, accelerated cooling, and controlled rolling. It applies intermediate cooling of rolled stock on УОВТ from 820–870 °C to 700–750 °C after the first five passes, then returns the stock to the finishing stand. The last three passes to final thickness use relative reductions up to 10%, with total reduction not less than 30%. It is a process route from Row 5, table cell C1, and is linked to the overall steel rolling process. [Data: Entities (1640, 1720, 1418); Relationships (3332, 3505, 3517, 3522, 3524, +more)]\"},{\"summary\":\"КПУО combines high-temperature КП with accelerated cooling\",\"explanation\":\"КПУО denotes high-temperature controlled rolling with accelerated cooling, designated by combining high-temperature КП and УО. It has been considered for implementation at mills 3000 and 3600 under various schemes. Its lower end-rolling temperature limit may be 730–800 °C, and its temperature interval defines where УОВТ cooling rates meet requirements. КПУО affects mill productivity through reduction of hold time, and it has cooling-rate and cooling-duration requirements. [Data: Entities (1356, 1610, 1630, 1593, 1796, +more); Relationships (3260, 2980, 3262, 3208, 3248, +more)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Mill implementation centers on mills 3000 and 3600\",\"explanation\":\"Proposed КПУО parameters were considered for mills 3000 and 3600. Mill 3000 at MK im. Ilyicha is used for controlled rolling of skelp and can preliminarily cool intermediates to 750–820 °C using shlepper cooling beds; its rolling rate is almost twice that of mill 3600. Mill 3600 at MK Azovstal, Mariupol, has conditions for accelerated cooling of rolled stock and achieves preliminary cooling to 750–820 °C by holding on an intermediate roller table. These mills are directly linked to КПУО implementation and mill productivity considerations. [Data: Entities (1624, 1631, 1578, 1393, 1646); Relationships (3315, 3316, 3240, 3248)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Sheet rolling duration and productivity drive process selection\",\"explanation\":\"The duration of technological operations, especially sheet rolling in the finishing stand, is a key reason КП+УО is preferred. Mill productivity is primarily determined by rolling rate, specifically the rolling rate of sheets. It decreases under certain regimes and during low-temperature controlled rolling, and is affected by reduction of hold time in КПУО/КП+УО schemes. Sheets include low-pearlite steel plates with thicknesses from 10–32 mm, including specific 16–20 mm and 18.7 mm variants, evaluated under mill 3600 conditions. [Data: Entities (1646, 1393, 1388, 1355); Relationships (3346, 3248, 2965)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Low-temperature КП provides a comparison baseline\",\"explanation\":\"Low-temperature КП is a controlled-rolling scheme with an accepted temperature range of 690–740 °C, used for plates 16–20 mm thick from steels such as 09–10Г2ФБ. It is compared with high-temperature КП and КПУО, and with КП+УО in relation to sheet rolling duration. The low-temperature variant is associated with sheets/plates and serves as the baseline against which the 150 s duration reduction for КП+УО is measured. [Data: Entities (1355, 1388, 1686, 1700); Relationships (2965, 3460)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Sulfur content affects separation behavior\",\"explanation\":\"Sulfur (S) content in steel influences manganese sulfide (MnS) inclusions and the initiation of separation. Even extremely low S content can still be associated with separation, and separation can occur even when MnS is only occasionally present. This links steel chemistry to quality or defect risks in the rolling community, although the provided data focuses on the S–separation relationship rather than a specific mill or scheme. [Data: Entities (744, 778); Relationships (1497, 1530)]\"},{\"summary\":\"Table parameters define the КП+УО temperature and duration window\",\"explanation\":\"The Row 6 route for КП+УО is associated with table parameters C7=820–870 °C, C8=730–800 °C, C9=8, C11=720–790 °C, C12=500–550 °C, and C13=75–80 s. These values specify the temperature and timing regime for the preferred scheme, complementing the qualitative description of finishing-stand rolling and accelerated cooling. They provide the quantitative process window used to compare КП+УО with other controlled-rolling routes. [Data: Entities (1565, 1738, 1741, 1743, 1750, +more); Relationships (3534, 3535, 3536, 3538, 3539, +more)]\"}],\"rating\":6.0,\"rating_explanation\":\"The impact severity is moderate-to-high because these controlled-rolling and accelerated-cooling schemes are industrially important for steel plate production, mill productivity, and product quality, but the community is technical rather than a direct security threat.\"}"}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 9428, "completion_tokens": 7204, "total_tokens": 16632, "compute_duration_seconds": 32.67745542526245, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}